<BaseLayout title="Assisted Self Publishing Services" description="Prepare and publish your book through established self publishing platforms while keeping your publishing identity under your control.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Publishing assistance" title="Independent publication, with professional support around it." intro="We help you prepare and publish your book through established self publishing and distribution platforms while keeping your publishing identity under your control." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell editorial-split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The model</p><h2>Assistance without acquisition.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Author Vista may prepare files, metadata, descriptions, categories and submission materials, then guide or assist the author through the selected platform’s publishing process.</p><p>Depending on the project, intended platform support may include Amazon KDP, IngramSpark, Lulu, Apple Books, Kobo and Barnes & Noble where available.</p><p>The author should hold and control publishing accounts wherever the platform permits. Author Vista does not claim to act as a distributor or hold official platform partnerships.</p></div></div><div class="service-motif motif-path" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>01</b></div></div></section>
  <section class="section surface-mist"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Publishing preparation</p><div class="principles"><div class="principle"><h3>Production files</h3><p>Approved print and ebook files prepared to the chosen platform’s requirements.</p></div><div class="principle"><h3>Metadata guidance</h3><p>Descriptions, categories, keywords and ISBN considerations discussed in context.</p></div><div class="principle"><h3>Account guidance</h3><p>Support setting up or working within author controlled accounts.</p></div><div class="principle"><h3>Submission assistance</h3><p>Guidance through platform steps without implying guaranteed acceptance or reach.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="answer-block"><p class="eyebrow">A direct answer</p><h2>Does Author Vista take royalties?</h2><p>No. Author Vista charges for professional services and does not claim an ongoing share of royalties generated through the author’s publishing accounts. Contractual treatment of ISBNs, licensed assets, editable files and specialist rights must be confirmed before engagement.</p></div></div></section>
  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
